## Quick reference — the only commands you need

```powershell
python dbtool.py ping                          # check connection
python dbtool.py tables [--like "PAT%"]        # list tables/views
python dbtool.py describe TABLE                 # columns + PK
python dbtool.py query "SELECT ..."             # read-only query
python dbtool.py query "SELECT ... :x" --bind x=VALUE   # with a bound value
# add --format tsv for big results, --limit N to change the row cap
```
Remember: identifiers (table/column names) go inside the SQL text; only literal **values**
use `--bind`.
